<section class="fragment-benchmark" data-artifact="benchmark" data-slice="engine-core" data-mode="baseline">
  <table class="bm-metrics">
    <thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Budget</th><th>Unit</th><th>Direction</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>budget.match_wall_ms</td><td>2000</td><td>ms</td><td>lower is better</td></tr>
      <tr><td>budget.ticks_per_s</td><td>135000</td><td>ticks/s</td><td>higher is better</td></tr>
      <tr><td>budget.batch_1000_wall_min</td><td>30</td><td>min</td><td>lower is better</td></tr>
      <tr><td>tripwire.cpu_regression_pct</td><td>10</td><td>%</td><td>lower is better</td></tr>
      <tr><td>tripwire.memory_regression_pct</td><td>25</td><td>%</td><td>lower is better</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">Greenfield baseline</div><div class="callout-body">No code exists and no measurement ran. The budget column holds the NFR-1 budget and the tripwires from the shape. Compare mode, run by verify after implement, reports the first measured medians against these values.</div></aside>
  <style>
    .fragment-benchmark .bm-metrics { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem; }
    .fragment-benchmark .bm-metrics th, .fragment-benchmark .bm-metrics td { text-align: left; padding: 6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(127,127,127,0.25); }
    .fragment-benchmark .callout { margin-top: 12px; }
  </style>
  <script>
    (function () {
      var root = document.currentScript.closest('.fragment-benchmark');
      var metrics = root ? root.querySelectorAll('.bm-metrics tbody tr').length : 0;
      window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('sdlc:fragment-ready', { detail: { name: 'benchmark', artifact: 'benchmark', counts: { metrics: metrics, regressions: 0, improvements: 0 } } }));
    })();
  </script>
</section>
